  "body": "## What changed\n\nRequested by @spikeypineapple on #616. Smoothing differs per control, and the \"auto\" behaviour is maximum accuracy on finishing, with roughing aggressiveness following the stock left. The design was posted on the issue before code.\n\n- **The option:** **\"Smoothing per operation\"**, a new document post option (`PostOptions.smoothing`), **off by default**.\n  - **Off:** no smoothing PARAM is in the stream, so every program, and the `postOptions` object, is **byte-identical**.\n  - **Saving:** the additive `smoothing` project key, absent when off. Undoable through `SetPostOptions`, and offered as a checkbox under the post picker for every mill post.\n- **On, each operation states its ask** (`app::smoothing::of`) as `PARAM Smoothing <mm>` + `PARAM SmoothingMode finish|rough`:\n  - **finish:** an op with a contour tolerance and no stock left asks **half** its tolerance (the control's deviation stacks on the verified path);\n  - **rough:** an op leaving stock asks **stock × 0.2, capped at 0.25 mm, never more than that fifth** (no floor);\n  - **nothing:** drilling, tapping, probing, threading, facing and the lathe kinds ask nothing.\n- **Each mill post writes its control's words** after the section preamble and **undoes them at the section end**, so no tolerance leaks:\n\n  | Post | On | Off |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Tormach / LinuxCNC | `G64 P<tol>` | the header's `G64 P0.001` / `P0.025` |\n  | Fanuc | one note \"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - G5.1 STATES NO TOLERANCE\" (G5.1 has no tolerance word; review of #635) | none |\n  | Haas | `G187 P3\\|P1 E<tol>` | `G187` |\n  | Siemens 840D | `CYCLE832(<tol>,_FINISH\\|_ROUGH,1)` | `CYCLE832()` |\n  | Heidenhain (ISO) | `G62 T<tol>` | `G62` |\n  | Mazak | one note \"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - NO MAZAK FORM STATED\" (no guessed word) | none |\n\n- **Fanuc writes nothing yet:** `G5.1 Q1` states no tolerance, so it can't be held to the op's ask. A bounded form can follow with #614's Doosan sample. Decision record: `docs/decisions/616-smoothing.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs`, 4/4:**\n  - `off_is_byte_identical_and_writes_no_smoothing_word`: every mill post.\n  - `each_dialect_writes_its_words_and_undoes_them_at_the_section_end`: finish and rough per dialect; the words are stated before the first cut and reset after.\n  - `mazak_names_the_ask_once_and_writes_no_guessed_word`\n  - `finish_ops_ask_their_tolerance_and_rough_ops_ask_from_their_stock`: including the clamp ends and drill → none.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** post and app suites pass after the follow-up commit. The first run caught `lathe_post_g76` pinning the whole `postOptions` object; the key is now omitted when off. The only ui reds are the 3 known GPU-adapter tests (#615 / #623).\n- **Named, all with the option off:**\n\n  | Suite | Passed |\n  |---|---|\n  | conformance | 6 |\n  | golden_cl | 23 |\n  | posting | 17 |\n  | tormach_post | 10 |\n  | fanuc_post | 11 |\n  | heidenhain_block_form | 4 |\n  | sinumerik_safe_retract | 3 |\n  | coolant | 7 |\n  | after_op | 10 |\n  | project_roundtrip | 69 |\n  | per_op_files | 9 |\n  | lathe_post_g76 | 5 |\n  | ui structural / post_options / after_op | 5 |\n\n- **Clippy** on post, app and ui with `-D warnings`: clean. **No golden or snapshot changed.**\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA run on a real control or simulator with smoothing on. PathPilot Hub can check the Tormach `G64 P` per section. The Haas `G187`, Siemens `CYCLE832` and Heidenhain `G62` words come from public documentation and haven't been run on a control. That's why the option is opt-in.\n\nChangelog: An opt-in \"Smoothing per operation\" post option writes each control's smoothing mode per operation (finish tolerance or a roughing deviation from the stock left): G64 P, G5.1, G187, CYCLE832, G62 (#616)\n\nFixes #616\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
